# Frozen evaluation evidence is bound by the SHA-256 of its raw bytes:
# datasets, manifests, reports, and the runners that hash their own source.
# Any end-of-line translation changes those bytes, so a default Windows
# checkout (core.autocrlf=true) would rewrite LF to CRLF and every identity
# check would fail with a SHA mismatch. Pin the working tree to LF here so
# the evidence chain reproduces on every platform.
#
# `text eol=lf` rather than `-text`: bytes stay identical to the blob, and
# the files remain diffable instead of being treated as binary.
benchmarks/** text eol=lf
